{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A multiline registered credential can be reconstructed unredacted in saved failure excerpts and model feedback, but such credentials are very uncommon."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Output truncation can leave a credential fragment that redaction cannot match, exposing that fragment in saved gate output."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"test","trigger":"normal","reason":"The new assertions pass even when gate output is unredacted because the verify prompt never includes that output."}]}